# CR 616.1, on an instruction to draw (CR 121.2a). Bot1 controls Quantum Riddler and a token copy of it, with an empty
# hand, and the token's "When this creature enters, draw a card" resolves. Both Riddlers' "if you would draw one or
# more cards, you draw that many cards plus one instead" apply to that one instruction, so the affected player — the
# one who would draw — chooses which applies first. The other still applies afterwards (CR 616.1f: no card has been
# drawn yet, so the hand is still empty), and the instruction for one card draws three.
#
# The question used to be addressed to nobody: the instruction to draw was the one event the pipeline could not name
# an affected player for, and a server refuses to send a prompt to seat 0.
#
# Everything happens on turn 1 so that the hand is empty when the draw is made: an Island, three Black Lotuses and a
# Mox leave the Riddler and Three Steps Ahead, the Riddler is cast, and the copy is made in response to its enters
# trigger. The token's trigger is then on top (three cards, hand of 0), and the original's resolves second with three
# cards in hand, where neither effect applies, and draws one.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Black Lotus
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Quantum Riddler
Three Steps Ahead
Mountain
Forest
Swamp
Plains
Island x10

